{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_103","type":"agent_message","text":"Implemented the two Story 2 fixes.\n\nThe project shell now exposes a user-editable metadata form for each source row in [source-attachment-section.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/apps/platform/client/features/projects/source-attachment-section.ts), wired through [project-shell-page.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/apps/platform/client/features/projects/project-shell-page.ts), [shell-app.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/apps/platform/client/app/shell-app.ts), and [bootstrap.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/apps/platform/client/app/bootstrap.ts). It sends the existing PATCH request and replaces the updated row in store state without reloading the full shell.\n\nOn the server side, update-by-`sourceAttachmentId` no longer depends on the capped project attachment listing. I added a direct by-id project-scoped lookup in [convex/sourceAttachments.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/convex/sourceAttachments.ts) and [platform-store.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts), then switched [source-management.service.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-management.service.ts) to use that path while keeping project access and project-membership validation intact. I also updated the app wiring cast in [app.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/apps/platform/server/app.ts).\n\nFocused proofs were added in [project-router.test.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/tests/service/client/project-router.test.ts) for the PATCH + in-place row update, and in [source-management-service.test.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/tests/service/server/source-management-service.test.ts) for updating an attachment beyond a simulated 200-row cap.\n\nVerification: `corepack pnpm run green-verify` passed."}}
